WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

01:52.590 --> 01:59.600
<b>The World’s Membrane is Full of Holes</b>

02:12.580 --> 02:15.480
<b>I don’t get what you’re saying.</b>

02:15.480 --> 02:18.350
<b>Yeah. You wouldn’t.</b>

02:18.350 --> 02:19.990
<b>Are you trying to pick a fight with me?</b>

02:19.990 --> 02:21.360
<b>Not at all.</b>

02:21.360 --> 02:22.660
<b>But–</b>

02:22.660 --> 02:24.330
<b>It’s all right.</b>

02:24.330 --> 02:25.490
<b>What?</b>

02:25.490 --> 02:27.190
<b>It’s fine.</b>

02:28.330 --> 02:30.200
<b>Hey, Kisa!</b>

02:30.200 --> 02:32.170
<b>I have some things I need to
talk to him about anyway.</b>

02:33.870 --> 02:35.140
<b>Is that so?</b>

02:35.140 --> 02:36.800
<b>Sorry.</b>

02:36.810 --> 02:37.870
<b>Why are you...?!</b>

02:37.870 --> 02:42.340
<b>In the first place, if you’re going to apologize,
don’t start off by speaking nonsense!</b>

02:42.340 --> 02:45.250
<b>Geez. You both have loose screws.</b>

02:47.080 --> 02:49.150
<b>Why are you here?</b>

02:50.320 --> 02:54.290
<b>Dosshiru and Shisshin,
who were with me back then...</b>

02:54.290 --> 02:58.760
<b>...traveled over 100 km to join me
in Yokohama.</b>

02:59.930 --> 03:01.860
<b>They were brought here by a cat.</b>

03:01.860 --> 03:03.000
<b>A cat?</b>

03:03.570 --> 03:06.500
<b>Her name’s Old Lady Okaka.</b>

03:06.500 --> 03:07.640
<b>What’s that?</b>

03:07.640 --> 03:09.040
<b>A cat.</b>

03:09.040 --> 03:12.510
<b>If you’re asking how she got that name,
that’s a whole nother story.</b>

03:12.510 --> 03:15.380
<b>Who cares about some cat’s name?</b>

03:16.480 --> 03:18.580
<b>100 km is a long way.</b>

03:18.580 --> 03:23.510
<b>I’ve been pondering what kind of feelings that cat must’ve had...</b>

03:23.510 --> 03:26.590
<b>...while walking the whole way here...</b>

03:26.590 --> 03:28.320
<b>...and the reason why she had to.</b>

03:28.320 --> 03:29.820
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:29.830 --> 03:32.560
<b>It was because of some circumstances on my side.</b>

03:33.300 --> 03:39.030
<b>But looking at what Dosshiru and Shisshin
did to your... Bun-chan, was it?</b>

03:42.040 --> 03:49.740
<b>What they did... is a truth that can’t ever
be erased, and as to why it happened...</b>

03:49.750 --> 03:50.750
<b>Don’t say any more.</b>

03:50.750 --> 03:54.010
<b>Kisa! Let’s go back.</b>

03:54.020 --> 04:00.220
<b>I can’t change the past, but I felt that there
was still something left for me to do.</b>

04:01.020 --> 04:03.590
<b>So I decided to wait for you.</b>

04:05.560 --> 04:08.200
<b>Not just at specific times...</b>

04:08.860 --> 04:10.630
<b>...but to wait for you proactively.</b>

04:11.870 --> 04:15.670
<b>I had a friend who did the same for me.</b>

04:16.710 --> 04:21.510
<b>Even if you call it proactive or whatever,
the act of waiting is passive.</b>

04:21.510 --> 04:24.880
<b>That’s why I’m here now.</b>

04:26.480 --> 04:29.450
<b>And that’s why you came, Tanigawa-san.</b>

04:52.570 --> 04:53.570
<b>Makki.</b>

04:55.580 --> 04:57.280
<b>Where’s Kisa and Riezo?</b>

04:57.280 --> 04:59.450
<b>I can’t get in touch with them.</b>

04:59.450 --> 05:02.720
<b>They’re probably under that, though.</b>

05:03.520 --> 05:04.890
<b>Riezo, too?</b>

05:04.890 --> 05:09.620
<b>Once someone like Tanigawa sets her mind on
something, she’ll see it through no matter what.</b>

05:05.380 --> 05:13.860
<b>Due to the effects of the Colossus,</b>

05:05.380 --> 05:13.860
<b>both the upper and lower railway</b>

05:05.380 --> 05:13.860
<b>tracks are temporarily out of operation.</b>

05:05.380 --> 05:13.860
<b>Notice</b>

05:05.380 --> 05:13.860
<b>- Station Chief</b>

05:09.620 --> 05:12.260
<b>And I don’t think Rieko-chan would
let her go under that thing alone.</b>

05:14.460 --> 05:18.770
<b>Since I can’t contact either of them,
don’t you think that means they’re together?</b>

05:18.770 --> 05:20.100
<b>I see.</b>

05:20.100 --> 05:21.870
<b>All right.</b>

05:21.870 --> 05:24.410
<b>Are you still going, even though it’s off-limits?</b>

05:27.510 --> 05:29.380
<b>You’ve changed, Makki.</b>

05:31.680 --> 05:34.050
<b>Of course I have.
A lot’s happened.</b>

05:35.350 --> 05:42.320
<b>I don’t want Kisa to have any more
painful or sad memories.</b>

05:44.330 --> 05:46.930
<b>Even if I go, I’m not sure what I can do.</b>

05:46.930 --> 05:50.360
<b>But if I don’t go, I know that nothing can happen.</b>

05:50.370 --> 05:54.900
<b>That’s why... if Kisa’s there, I’ll go.</b>

05:54.900 --> 05:56.400
<b>Yeah.</b>

05:56.410 --> 05:58.070
<b>Are you going?</b>

05:58.770 --> 06:00.810
<b>I’ll be right behind you.</b>

06:00.810 --> 06:02.940
<b>I’m sure we’ll be able to meet up again.</b>

06:02.940 --> 06:05.850
<b>But right now, I have to wait for Sukawara-san.</b>

06:05.850 --> 06:09.250
<b>You really have changed.</b>

06:09.250 --> 06:10.180
<b>Wait.</b>

06:11.290 --> 06:15.420
<b>There’s a policeman straight ahead,
so go in from the Kannai side.</b>

06:15.420 --> 06:17.460
<b>Mention these things sooner.</b>

06:18.830 --> 06:25.300
<b>Oh, and speaking of changing, it seems like
Kisa’s Bun-chan changed into a fairy.</b>

06:29.340 --> 06:30.770
<b>Hey.</b>

06:32.140 --> 06:33.870
<b>There’s something I want you to see.</b>

06:42.580 --> 06:45.090
<b>This one... was born.</b>

06:50.230 --> 06:52.530
<b>I just thought of a name for it...</b>

06:53.700 --> 06:55.000
<b>Pou-chan.</b>

06:55.830 --> 06:58.070
<b>Because it shimmers with a “pou”
sound, it’ll be Pou-chan.</b>

06:59.130 --> 07:01.870
<b>This... is the type that was being
chased back then.</b>

07:01.870 --> 07:05.010
<b>Huh? What do you mean?</b>

07:05.010 --> 07:07.540
<b>So you also saw something.</b>

07:07.540 --> 07:09.310
<b>I did...</b>

07:10.110 --> 07:12.380
<b>One like this was being chased by pale blue lights...</b>

07:12.380 --> 07:17.280
<b>They looked like the ones drawn on
that underpass in Sakuragi Town.</b>

07:17.290 --> 07:19.420
<b>But...</b>

07:19.420 --> 07:21.090
<b>Are you absolutely sure of that?</b>

07:21.090 --> 07:24.390
<b>Do I have any reason to lie?</b>

07:24.390 --> 07:25.260
<b>I guess not.</b>

07:26.090 --> 07:29.600
<b>But that would mean... it’s the opposite of Bun-chan.</b>

07:30.800 --> 07:32.500
<b>Since Bun-chan was...</b>

07:49.180 --> 07:49.850
<b>No...!</b>

07:53.590 --> 07:56.320
<b>Hey... isn’t this bad?</b>

07:56.930 --> 07:58.790
<b>No...</b>

07:59.800 --> 08:01.530
<b>Don’t leave me alone again...</b>

08:01.530 --> 08:03.430
<b>Don’t take Pou-chan away from me, too!</b>

08:04.900 --> 08:07.600
<b>Kisa. We should get away from here.</b>

08:09.500 --> 08:10.910
<b>It’s dangerous.</b>

08:12.810 --> 08:14.580
<b>Hey, you should also get away...!</b>

08:17.110 --> 08:18.550
<b>Come on!</b>

08:44.610 --> 08:45.670
<b>You guys are...</b>

08:50.210 --> 08:51.510
<b>You wanna fight?!</b>

08:55.620 --> 08:56.780
<b>What?</b>

09:02.590 --> 09:04.730
<b>You want me to come with you?</b>

09:21.540 --> 09:23.540
<b>Still no good, huh?</b>

09:23.510 --> 09:24.980
<b>Incoming</b>

09:23.510 --> 09:24.980
<b>Sukawara-san</b>

09:25.650 --> 09:27.250
<b>Hello?</b>

09:27.250 --> 09:28.480
<b>Where are you right now?</b>

09:28.480 --> 09:29.780
<b>In front of the station.</b>

09:29.790 --> 09:31.590
<b>Are you here already?</b>

09:31.590 --> 09:35.020
<b>Not yet. Because of the roadblock,
I had to leave the taxi.</b>

09:35.020 --> 09:37.320
<b>Right now I’m running over there and–</b>

09:39.460 --> 09:41.430
<b>Out of Area</b>

09:55.010 --> 09:56.040
<b>Where are you going?</b>

09:56.040 --> 09:57.580
<b>We have to get away from here.</b>

09:58.050 --> 09:58.880
<b>Why?</b>

09:58.880 --> 10:00.310
<b>Enough already! Hurry!</b>

10:01.820 --> 10:02.820
<b>Kisa?</b>

10:04.150 --> 10:05.420
<b>I’m not going.</b>

10:05.420 --> 10:07.050
<b>It’s dangerous!</b>

10:07.060 --> 10:09.060
<b>I wonder about that.</b>

10:09.060 --> 10:10.990
<b>Is it really?</b>

10:10.990 --> 10:14.030
<b>Use some common sense!</b>

10:14.030 --> 10:20.670
<b>If we used common sense,
would this all still exist?</b>

10:25.110 --> 10:27.040
<b>You’re just evading the issue.</b>

10:27.040 --> 10:28.680
<b>No...</b>

10:28.680 --> 10:30.880
<b>I’m not trying to do that...</b>

10:30.880 --> 10:31.750
<b>Umm...</b>

10:31.750 --> 10:33.150
<b>I have to agree.</b>

10:35.120 --> 10:37.390
<b>With Tanigawa-san.</b>

10:37.390 --> 10:40.050
<b>I don’t think we can use
common sense with this thing.</b>

